5,1,1,talk,Daisuke,,I think we should look at the incident logs and the time lost to copying records.,"{""words"":16,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
6,1,1,talk,May,,I’d like to check the staffing of the coordination group and in-house developer availability.,"{""words"":14,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
7,1,1,talk,Shunichi,,I want to verify network coverage at customer plants and in-house developer availability.,"{""words"":13,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
8,1,1,talk,Ryuji,,"I’ll examine the capital budget and software allowance, plus the vendor licence pricing versus fixed-fee work.","{""words"":16,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
9,1,1,talk,Kenji,,I want to see the outcomes of the last three internal rollouts and the record of cross-unit standardization efforts.,"{""words"":19,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
10,1,2,talk,Daisuke,,"@May, do you think the coordination group’s current load will actually absorb any new project work?","{""words"":16,""mentions"":[""May""],""raw_differs"":false}"
11,1,2,talk,May,,"@Daisuke, that’s exactly why I’m checking. If the same two people are already drowning, adding more work is just asking for a breakdown.","{""words"":23,""mentions"":[""Daisuke""],""raw_differs"":false}"
12,1,2,talk,Shunichi,,"@Ryuji, if the capital line is frozen, how do we justify any proposal that isn’t purely recurring software?","{""words"":18,""mentions"":[""Ryuji""],""raw_differs"":false}"
13,1,2,talk,Ryuji,,"@Shunichi, I’m checking the allowance. If the capital line is frozen, we must rely on the recurring software budget, which still has room.","{""words"":23,""mentions"":[""Shunichi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
14,1,2,talk,Kenji,,"@Shunichi, I’m looking at past rollouts to see which projects actually survived their first year.","{""words"":15,""mentions"":[""Shunichi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
15,1,3,talk,Daisuke,,"@Kenji, do you think the past failures were due to the tools themselves, or just how we tried to force them onto the floor?","{""words"":24,""mentions"":[""Kenji""],""raw_differs"":false}"
16,1,3,talk,May,,"@Daisuke, I suspect it’s the people. If the tool demands daily effort from exhausted staff, it dies. I’m checking who’s left to carry it.","{""words"":24,""mentions"":[""Daisuke""],""raw_differs"":false}"
17,1,3,talk,Shunichi,,"@May, I’m verifying if the technical groundwork is even feasible. If the network fails, your staffing concerns are moot.","{""words"":19,""mentions"":[""May""],""raw_differs"":false}"
18,1,3,talk,Ryuji,,"@Shunichi, feasibility is only half the battle. If the recurring allowance is the only open door, we must ensure the proposal fits that specific financial constraint.","{""words"":26,""mentions"":[""Shunichi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
19,1,3,talk,Kenji,,"@Daisuke, I suspect the failures came from forcing broad tools on tired staff. The narrow ones for specific trades survived.","{""words"":20,""mentions"":[""Daisuke""],""raw_differs"":false}"
20,1,4,talk,Daisuke,,"@Kenji, that matches what I see in the logs. The narrow tools survived because they didn’t demand extra effort from tired people.","{""words"":22,""mentions"":[""Kenji""],""raw_differs"":false}"
21,1,4,talk,May,,"@Shunichi, if the network is down half the time, your app is just a fancy paper form. I’m checking if we even have the people to maintain it.","{""words"":28,""mentions"":[""Shunichi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
22,1,4,talk,Shunichi,,"@May, I’m checking the signal. If half the sites lose coverage, a mobile app is useless. I need to know if the groundwork is even possible.","{""words"":26,""mentions"":[""May""],""raw_differs"":false}"
23,1,4,talk,Ryuji,,"@May, the financial path is clear. We must fit within the recurring software allowance, as the capital line is frozen.","{""words"":20,""mentions"":[""May""],""raw_differs"":false}"
24,1,4,talk,Kenji,,"@Ryuji, agreed. But if the capital line is frozen, we must ensure the recurring cost doesn’t balloon with every new user added.","{""words"":22,""mentions"":[""Ryuji""],""raw_differs"":false}"
