35,2,1,talk,Daisuke,,"@May, the logs show eleven misrouted deliveries this year, all from duplicate addresses. It’s a simple fix, not a grand gesture.","{""words"":21,""mentions"":[""May""],""raw_differs"":false}"
36,2,1,talk,May,,"@Daisuke, that’s a data problem, not a staffing one. But my check shows the coordination group is empty, and our developers are stuck until Q3.","{""words"":25,""mentions"":[""Daisuke""],""raw_differs"":false}"
37,2,1,talk,Shunichi,,"@May, the signal is worse than I feared. Half the sites lose coverage for whole afternoons. A mobile app is technically impossible without major infrastructure changes.","{""words"":26,""mentions"":[""May""],""raw_differs"":false}"
38,2,1,talk,Ryuji,,"@Shunichi, that confirms the capital freeze. We cannot fund infrastructure. We must stick to the recurring software allowance, which is the only viable path forward.","{""words"":25,""mentions"":[""Shunichi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
39,2,1,talk,Kenji,,"@Shunichi, that’s a hard constraint. But my review shows the narrow, single-trade tools survived, while the broad ones died. We need a proposal that fits that pattern.","{""words"":27,""mentions"":[""Shunichi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
40,2,2,talk,Daisuke,,"@May, if the developers are stuck until Q3, who builds the fix for those duplicate addresses? I’m worried we’re stuck.","{""words"":20,""mentions"":[""May""],""raw_differs"":false}"
41,2,2,talk,May,,"@Daisuke, nobody. The developers are locked in until Q3, and the coordination group is empty. We can’t build anything new right now.","{""words"":22,""mentions"":[""Daisuke""],""raw_differs"":false}"
42,2,2,talk,Shunichi,,"@May, that’s the reality. No developers, no network. We can’t build. We can only select what already works or requires zero new code.","{""words"":23,""mentions"":[""May""],""raw_differs"":false}"
43,2,2,talk,Ryuji,,"@Shunichi, precisely. If we cannot build, we must select a tool that fits the recurring allowance without demanding new capital or developer time.","{""words"":23,""mentions"":[""Shunichi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
44,2,2,talk,Kenji,,"@Ryuji, agreed. But if we can’t build, we must pick a tool that doesn’t need new code. My data shows narrow, single-trade tools survive; broad ones die.","{""words"":27,""mentions"":[""Ryuji""],""raw_differs"":false}"
45,2,3,talk,Daisuke,,"@May, if we can’t build, how do we fix the duplicate addresses? The logs show that’s where the real daily pain is.","{""words"":22,""mentions"":[""May""],""raw_differs"":false}"
46,2,3,talk,May,,"@Daisuke, we don’t fix it with code. We fix it with process. The hub is a repository, not an app. It’s about organizing what we already have, not building new tech.","{""words"":31,""mentions"":[""Daisuke""],""raw_differs"":false}"
47,2,3,talk,Shunichi,,"@May, a repository still needs someone to maintain it. With no developers and an empty coordination group, who updates the records?","{""words"":21,""mentions"":[""May""],""raw_differs"":false}"
48,2,3,talk,Ryuji,,"@Shunichi, maintenance is a recurring cost, not capital. If the allowance covers it, we proceed. The question is whether the process is sustainable without new hires.","{""words"":26,""mentions"":[""Shunichi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
49,2,3,talk,Kenji,,"@Shunichi, that’s the risk. But my data shows standardization efforts fail without an owner. We need a proposal that doesn’t rely on a dedicated team to survive.","{""words"":27,""mentions"":[""Shunichi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
50,2,4,talk,Daisuke,,"@May, if it’s just organizing existing records, does that actually stop the daily copying I see in the logs? I need to know if it solves the real problem.","{""words"":29,""mentions"":[""May""],""raw_differs"":false}"
51,2,4,talk,May,,"@Daisuke, yes. One searchable catalog means you stop copying details that already exist. It directly attacks the hour of daily waste you found.","{""words"":23,""mentions"":[""Daisuke""],""raw_differs"":false}"
52,2,4,talk,Shunichi,,"@May, a repository is just a database. Without developers to build the interface or staff to maintain it, it’s just a digital filing cabinet. Who actually does the work?","{""words"":29,""mentions"":[""May""],""raw_differs"":false}"
53,2,4,talk,Ryuji,,"@Shunichi, the allowance covers the software, not the labor. If the clerks can maintain it within their current duties, it fits. We cannot hire new staff.","{""words"":26,""mentions"":[""Shunichi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
54,2,4,talk,Kenji,,"@Shunichi, valid point. But my data shows narrow tools survive because they fit existing workflows. If the hub is just a catalog, it might work. If it’s a new system, it dies.","{""words"":32,""mentions"":[""Shunichi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
